# tagging a release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Separatrix in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Separatrix: quantum-inspired portfolio optimisation with exact ground truth, on-chain commitments, and quantum-primitive characterisation"
abstract: >-
  A pure-Rust simulated-bifurcation Ising/QUBO solver benchmarked against
  simulated annealing, parallel tempering, and exhaustive enumeration on a
  cardinality-constrained crypto portfolio study; a Solana program that
  commits and re-derives allocation objectives on-chain; a spending firewall
  for autonomous agents; and a characterisation of Dicke-state preparation
  with XY-ring mixers on all-to-all trapped-ion connectivity. Every reported
  number is labelled measured, estimated, or not run. No quantum advantage is
  claimed.
